            {
                "entry_id": "c52892a1-8f34-34c2-bbb1-92054567b147",
                "word": "genii",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90d03c2b-2736-388e-86ab-f4a7f994f2fe",
                        "entry_id": "c52892a1-8f34-34c2-bbb1-92054567b147",
                        "glosses": [
                            "plural of genius",
                            "Guardian spirits."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Roman"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e96844b-12b9-42f0-8fdd-9a4657bebd7c",
                                "sense_id": "90d03c2b-2736-388e-86ab-f4a7f994f2fe",
                                "text": "On the 11th Century glass bowl above, the painted figures—winged genii, nude athletes and brawny soldiers—resemble mythological characters but may be only lighthearted mimicry of ancient Greek or Roman subjects."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "018b8d40-c908-38ca-bf23-d22ca34de1ae",
                        "entry_id": "c52892a1-8f34-34c2-bbb1-92054567b147",
                        "glosses": [
                            "plural of genius",
                            "Any similar beings of other mythologies."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fca5e23b-06bb-45bf-b236-2b737da4bf37",
                                "sense_id": "018b8d40-c908-38ca-bf23-d22ca34de1ae",
                                "text": "\"According to the old wives' tales that are related about this race of genii who inhabit Iceland and its vicinity, they have a political form of government modelled after the same pattern as that which the inhabitants themselves are under."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ada5c54-6636-3958-a81f-d59906063cce",
                        "entry_id": "c52892a1-8f34-34c2-bbb1-92054567b147",
                        "glosses": [
                            "plural of genius",
                            "People possessing extraordinary intelligence or skill."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec0ce534-bc5b-4a6e-a71b-304c6620db24",
                                "sense_id": "3ada5c54-6636-3958-a81f-d59906063cce",
                                "text": "Quiz kids of Senior Class announced today. Jack Daniels, Valedictorian; Mary Lou Shaw, Salutatorian; Irvin Nachman, Third Honor Student; Boots Cumming, Highest Average, and Janet Davis, Second Highest Average. Just a bunch of genii that’s all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82db4620-4f0b-4682-92a5-3de6fdb04250",
                                "sense_id": "3ada5c54-6636-3958-a81f-d59906063cce",
                                "text": "It aint oftin that you’s git a more better group of genii as was collected this year at good old Melrose High. To the credit of they, it can be said them didn’t do nothin’."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41e50fe5-6820-4f62-aae7-cb99f3d812a1",
                                "sense_id": "3ada5c54-6636-3958-a81f-d59906063cce",
                                "text": "As Hutchinson saw it, his role was always “that of a student trying to learn quietly and unobtrusively from this extraordinary group of genii. G.B. and M.M. [Gregory Bateson and Margaret Mead] were of course close personal friends. Wiener liked to hear about any branch of science.[…]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea2f1277-ec73-4e9a-be86-d03ff02c4169",
                                "sense_id": "3ada5c54-6636-3958-a81f-d59906063cce",
                                "text": "As far as we’re concerned, having our piece of this country’s rich literary history is our birthright. As such, we have a list of literary demands. Because we are genii, we expect this won’t be a problem."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
